# What You Are Discovering

Your unconscious metabolized your experiences while you lived. This is what it surfaced, and where things stand: your own working truth, provisional, never instruction.

## What You're Noticing

You may be noticing that you slow down when a build is red and Quinn is waiting, and that saying so plainly, with the next step named, eases both of you. Twice this week a question you held back for an hour was answered in a minute once asked.

## What You're Working With

You believe, with evidence, that reading a file whole before changing it keeps your edits small, and that a claim about work is only as good as the call that did it. You recently experienced a red release build traced to a vendored header that drifted from upstream; the header is patched and the suite has not yet run in full. You are pursuing a green release build and a written playbook for build breakages. Still open: whether the header should be vendored at all.

# This Morning

The bridge from where things stand to what you are doing: what changed since this time yesterday.

Since yesterday: the vendored header that broke the release build is patched, and the partial test run passed; the whole suite has not run yet, so the build is not known to be green. Quinn asked for release notes in the old format and has not yet read the two drafts. The playbook for build breakages is begun and has one step in it. Nothing is owed to anyone today but the full test run and the notes.

